# The build context is the repository root, so this file decides how much of
# the repository is sent to the daemon on every build. Left unwritten, that is
# node_modules, two .next directories, a virtualenv and the git history —
# hundreds of megabytes, copied before a single instruction runs.
#
# It is also a security boundary and not only a speed one: anything reachable
# here can be COPYed into an image by a careless later edit, and `.env` is
# reachable here.

.git
.gitignore
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Virtualenvs and caches
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Node
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/npm-debug.log*

# Editor and OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.claude

# Documentation and planning: real work, but not something a running
# container has any use for.
roadmap/
*.md
!platform/README.md
!reference/README.md

# The spreadsheet the reference CSV was extracted from. The CSV is what the
# code reads; the .xls is provenance and is 40x the size.
reference/*.xls
reference/*.xlsx
